{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Final rebar-debug report: Problem was scheduled Windows sweep run 33426859481 failing before the test body because pytest put huge parametrized text into PYTEST_CURRENT_TEST. Proven root cause: `test_undecorated_text_is_byte_identical_to_the_bare_fitter` used bare tuples for 60k/75k text parameters, so collected nodeids exceeded Windows env-var value limit. Proof: collect-only measured 60171 and 75177 char env-shaped values before fix; RED test failed with the exact ValueError; after explicit ids collect showed over_limit=0 and focused module passed. Origin: commit 6724e79e8ff857b54dd36a62006a89445fc10ad6 / ticket 5931-78a3-95d2-44cd, recorded on close as caused_by with class plan_defect. Test: `test_pytest_current_test_values_fit_windows_environment`; mutation removing explicit ids in macOS sandbox returned it to RED. Fix: only added explicit short pytest ids; large product payloads/assertions unchanged. Scope/safety: test-only, no production callers, no deps, no test weakening. Siblings: candidate long-param nodeid sweep across large-payload tests found over_limit=0 beyond this site; parity axis N/A. Residual risk: unrelated local default-suite baseline failure in `test_atomic_completion_close.py::test_relevant_remote_rejection_never_places_candidate_on_shared_head`, accepted as out of scope because Gerrit Verified passed. Replication: Gerrit change 2469 merged; CI Verified+1 and LLM-Review+1."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788230097201404001,"uuid":"536a946a-842c-4236-ba01-27046f1f9912"}